Id: inet008i
Severity: INFO
Category: services
Check: check_inetd
References: xinetd(8); inetd(8); systemd.socket(5)

A super-server, xinetd or inetd (openbsd-inetd, inetutils-inetd), is
installed on this Linux host. The finding says whether it is enabled or
running and which services it serves (xinetd.d entries not disabled,
active inetd.conf lines); the insecure ones among them are judged by
inet005f and the small internal services by inet007w, so this is the
inventory, not a gap. No distribution installs a super-server by
default: systemd's socket units start the same services on demand.
Remove it if nothing needs it.
